      "text": "To find the remainder when the sum of the first five primes is divided by the sixth prime, we will:\n\n1. **List the prime numbers**: The first five prime numbers are 2, 3, 5, 7, and 11.\n2. **Calculate their sum**: Add these primes together:\n   \\[\n   2 + 3 + 5 + 7 + 11 = 28\n   \\]\n3. **Identify the sixth prime number**: The first six prime numbers are 2, 3, 5, 7, 11, and 13.\n4. **Calculate the remainder**: We need to find the remainder when 28 is divided by the sixth prime (13):\n   \\[\n   28 \\div 13\n   \\]\n   Performing the division:\n   \\[\n   28 \\div 13 \\approx 2.15384615...\n   \\]\n   The integer part of the quotient is 2. To find the exact remainder, subtract the product of the whole number part and 13 from 28:\n   \\[\n   28 - 2 \\times 13 = 28 - 26 = 2\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the remainder when the sum of the first five primes is divided by the sixth prime is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{2}\n\\]",
